      <span class="summit-eyebrow">01 / Acceptance</span>
      <h2>By visiting, you agree.</h2>
      <p>By using summithvac.example you agree to these terms. We may update them; the date at the top reflects the latest revision.</p>

      <span class="summit-eyebrow" style="display:block;margin-top:3rem">02 / Pricing on the site</span>
      <h2>Ranges, after rebates and tax credits.</h2>
      <p>Pricing tables on /pricing/ are typical residential ranges drawn from completed installs. They reflect post-rebate, post-IRA-25C pricing for qualifying customers and qualifying equipment. Your actual price depends on the load calc, your specific equipment selection, your home's existing infrastructure, and your eligibility for rebates/credits, which we determine during the estimate.</p>
      <p>The proposal we send is binding for 60 days. The site is not.</p>

      <span class="summit-eyebrow" style="display:block;margin-top:3rem">03 / Manual J load calculations</span>
      <h2>What the load calc tells us, and doesn't.</h2>
      <p>A Manual J load calculation per ACCA standards predicts the heat-loss and heat-gain of your home under design conditions. It is the industry standard for properly sizing HVAC equipment. It is not:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>A guarantee of energy bill savings (utility rates, occupant behavior, weather variability all matter).</li>
        <li>An audit of envelope performance independent of HVAC sizing (we'd recommend a separate energy audit for that).</li>
        <li>A substitute for a Manual D / S design for new construction (which we also offer separately).</li>
      </ul>

      <span class="summit-eyebrow" style="display:block;margin-top:3rem">04 / Equipment performance</span>
      <h2>SEER2 and HSPF ratings.</h2>
      <p>SEER2 and HSPF2 ratings are tested under standardized lab conditions. Real-world performance varies based on installation quality, duct sealing, refrigerant charge, climate, occupant behavior, and equipment cycling patterns. We commission every install to meet manufacturer-specified performance targets at the time of install, but we cannot warrant performance over the life of the equipment.</p>

      <span class="summit-eyebrow" style="display:block;margin-top:3rem">05 / Warranty</span>
      <h2>Two parts: workmanship + manufacturer.</h2>
      <p><strong>Workmanship warranty.</strong> Our installation labor is warranted for 2 years from commissioning. Defects caused by our installation (leaks at our joints, miswired controls, sizing errors) are repaired at no charge during this window.</p>
      <p><strong>Manufacturer warranty.</strong> Equipment is covered by the manufacturer for 5&ndash;10 years on parts (varies by model + registration). Compressors and heat exchangers typically carry longer warranties (10 years or lifetime). We register every install on your behalf to activate these warranties.</p>

      <span class="summit-eyebrow" style="display:block;margin-top:3rem">06 / Limitation of liability</span>
      <h2>Capped at install price.</h2>
      <p>To the extent permitted by Colorado law, our liability for any claim related to a project is capped at the contract price for that project. Summit carries $2M general liability and $2M workers' comp.</p>

